# Global saved skills

When a user adds a **custom skill** (via "Other — type your own") anywhere in Ledger, it must be remembered **globally** for every form that selects skills.

## Storage

- Use a single `localStorage` key: `ledger_saved_skills`
- Stored as an array of `{ module, skill }` objects
- All skill pickers must read from and write to this key (via `templates/macros/skills.html`)

## Behavior

- Custom skills are saved automatically when used — no opt-in checkbox
- Built-in module skills are never duplicated into saved storage
- Saved skills appear in a **Saved** optgroup for the matching module on every picker (daily goal, skill used)
- Pickers listen for `ledger-saved-skills-changed` and `storage` events to stay in sync

## When adding skill UI

- Reuse `templates/macros/skills.html` — do not create separate saved-skill storage
- Do not introduce alternate keys or server-side-only custom skill lists for picker UI
